<section class="fb-hero" id="height"><div class="fb-w"><div class="fb-hero-t"><p class="fb-pill">the sock guide for happy feet</p><h1>Good days start at your feet.</h1><p class="fb-lead">Footbed is an independent guide to socks. Find the right height for your shoes, the right size for your feet and the right fibre for your day, then keep them going wash after wash.</p></div>
<div class="fb-hero-g"><div class="fb-hp"><h2>Which sock height?</h2><div class="fb-hts" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Sock height"><label><input type="radio" name="ht" value="0"><span>No-show</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ht" value="1"><span>Ankle</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ht" value="2"><span>Quarter</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ht" value="3" checked><span>Crew</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ht" value="4"><span>Mid-calf</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="ht" value="5"><span>Knee-high</span></label></div><div class="fb-hv"><svg viewBox="0 0 160 260" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M58 20v150c0 10-4 14-14 20l-14 9c-14 9-10 41 12 41h66c18 0 28-16 28-34v-36l-2-150z" fill="#F3E3CE" stroke="#1F3A5F" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 4"/><path id="sk" d="" fill="#FF7A6B" stroke="#1F3A5F" stroke-width="3"/><path id="sk2" d="" fill="#1F3A5F"/></svg><div class="fb-ho" id="ht-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div><figure class="fb-hero-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1773837463640-e615246f7fa4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=620&q=75" alt="a pair of feet in white socks" width="520" height="620" fetchpriority="high"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="fb-s"><div class="fb-w fb-map"><div><p class="fb-pill">cushion map</p><h2>Where your foot needs help</h2><p class="fb-lead">Tap a zone on the foot. Good socks add padding or ventilation in different places depending on what you do.</p><div class="fb-zo" id="zn-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="fb-foot"><svg viewBox="0 0 220 400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M110 18c40 0 70 40 74 100 4 50-10 80-14 120-4 36 10 70 4 110-6 36-44 50-70 40-28-10-44-30-46-70-2-40 6-70 0-110-8-60 6-150 52-190z" fill="#FFE2C6" stroke="#1F3A5F" stroke-width="3"/><circle cx="72" cy="40" r="15" fill="#FFE2C6" stroke="#1F3A5F" stroke-width="3"/></svg><button class="fb-zn" data-z="0" style="left:55%;top:22%">Toes</button><button class="fb-zn" data-z="1" style="left:54%;top:38%">Ball</button><button class="fb-zn" data-z="2" style="left:28%;top:56%">Arch</button><button class="fb-zn" data-z="3" style="left:72%;top:62%">Sides</button><button class="fb-zn" data-z="4" style="left:50%;top:84%">Heel</button></div></div></section>

<section class="fb-s fb-mint" id="size"><div class="fb-w fb-sz"><div><p class="fb-pill">size converter</p><h2>Shoe size in, sock size out</h2><label for="sz-s">Your size system<select id="sz-s"><option value="usm">US men</option><option value="usw">US women</option><option value="uk">UK</option><option value="eu" selected>EU</option></select></label><label for="sz-n">Your shoe size<input id="sz-n" type="number" step="0.5" min="1" max="52" value="42"></label></div><div class="fb-szr"><div class="fb-ruler" id="sz-r" aria-hidden="true"><i data-s="S">S</i><i data-s="M">M</i><i data-s="L">L</i><i data-s="XL">XL</i><b id="sz-k"></b></div><div class="fb-szo" id="sz-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></section>

<section class="fb-s"><div class="fb-w"><div class="fb-fib-h"><div><p class="fb-pill">fibre deck</p><h2>What is your sock made of?</h2><p class="fb-lead">Most socks are blends. Flip a card to see what each fibre brings.</p></div><div class="fb-yarn"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794908471663-85f458b25a15?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="close-up of orange cable-knit wool" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794667757895-bcca90b6c7fe?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="colourful yarn cones on a wooden surface" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div><div class="fb-flips"><button class="fb-flip" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><span class="fb-fr"><b>Merino wool</b><em>Warm when cold, cool-ish when warm</em><i>Tap to flip</i></span><span class="fb-bk">Soft, fine wool that handles sweat well and resists odour. Great for hiking and winter; wash cool.</span></button><button class="fb-flip" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><span class="fb-fr"><b>Cotton</b><em>Soft and familiar</em><i>Tap to flip</i></span><span class="fb-bk">Comfortable for everyday wear but holds moisture, so feet stay damp in sport. Best in a blend.</span></button><button class="fb-flip" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><span class="fb-fr"><b>Nylon (polyamide)</b><em>The strength</em><i>Tap to flip</i></span><span class="fb-bk">Adds stretch, shape and durability. Most good socks contain some, often at the heel and toe.</span></button><button class="fb-flip" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><span class="fb-fr"><b>Polyester</b><em>Quick-drying</em><i>Tap to flip</i></span><span class="fb-bk">Moves sweat away fast and dries quickly. Common in running and gym socks.</span></button><button class="fb-flip" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><span class="fb-fr"><b>Elastane</b><em>The stretch</em><i>Tap to flip</i></span><span class="fb-bk">Just a few percent gives the cuff and arch its hug, so socks stay put.</span></button><button class="fb-flip" type="button" aria-pressed="false"><span class="fb-fr"><b>Bamboo viscose</b><em>Smooth and cool</em><i>Tap to flip</i></span><span class="fb-bk">A soft, silky fibre made from bamboo pulp. Feels cool; less hard-wearing than nylon blends.</span></button></div></div></section>

<section class="fb-s fb-navy"><div class="fb-w"><p class="fb-pill">for every kind of day</p><h2>Match the sock to the step</h2><div class="fb-acts"><article class="fb-act"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792601810007-96d64457ade9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=320&q=75" alt="a person wearing hiking boots and white socks" width="420" height="320" loading="lazy"></figure><div><h3>Hiking</h3><ul><li>Merino or wool blend</li><li>Cushioned heel and ball</li><li>Crew or mid-calf over the boot</li></ul></div></article><article class="fb-act"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792895007532-3bb7ef528e01?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=320&q=75" alt="argyle socks with brown leather dress shoes and pinstriped trousers" width="420" height="320" loading="lazy"></figure><div><h3>Office and dress</h3><ul><li>Thin, fine-knit cotton or wool</li><li>Mid-calf so no skin shows</li><li>Match trousers, or have fun</li></ul></div></article><article class="fb-act"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794728191085-b360157bad47?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=320&q=75" alt="a hiking boot on a forest floor covered in autumn leaves" width="420" height="320" loading="lazy"></figure><div><h3>Cold-weather walks</h3><ul><li>Thicker wool, full cushion</li><li>Room in the boot for the extra bulk</li><li>Carry a dry spare pair</li></ul></div></article></div></div></section>

<section class="fb-s"><div class="fb-w"><p class="fb-pill">laundry day</p><h2>Wash rules that make socks last</h2><div class="fb-wash"><div class="ok"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 14h36l-4 26H10z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M6 14q6 6 12 0t12 0 12 0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><text x="24" y="34" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="currentColor">30&deg;</text></svg><b>Wash cool</b><span>30&ndash;40&deg;C keeps fibres and elastic in shape.</span></div><div class="ok"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 6h16l4 8v28H12V14z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M20 22l8 8M28 22l-8 8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" transform="rotate(45 24 26)"/></svg><b>Turn inside out</b><span>Less pilling on the outside, cleaner on the inside.</span></div><div class="ok"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 16h40" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M12 16v18M24 16v22M36 16v16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/></svg><b>Air dry</b><span>Line or rack drying is kindest to elastic.</span></div><div class="no"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="8" y="8" width="32" height="32" rx="4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><circle cx="24" cy="24" r="10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M6 6l36 36" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/></svg><b>Hot tumble dry</b><span>Shrinks wool and tires out the stretch.</span></div><div class="no"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 40L24 10l16 30z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M6 6l36 36" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/></svg><b>Bleach</b><span>Weakens fibres and fades colour.</span></div><div class="no"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 34h28l-4-14H18z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M14 20l6-8h8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M6 6l36 36" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/></svg><b>Ironing</b><span>Not needed, and hard on elastic.</span></div></div><p class="fb-bub">&ldquo;Pair socks before washing, with a clip or tucked into each other, and the odd-sock mystery mostly disappears.&rdquo;</p></div></section>

